hoto/135216990.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/will-respond-to-legitimate-demands-macron-moves-to-ease-frances-student-unrest-vows-concrete-measures/articleshow/135216990.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/will-respond-to-legitimate-demands-macron-moves-to-ease-frances-student-unrest-vows-concrete-measures/articleshow/135216990.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T23:26:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135217227,imgsize-1607013.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chris Hemsworth bought a 10-acre Byron Bay estate for A$7 million; now it is a mega-mansion]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135199443.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a bold move away from Hollywood's hustle, Chris Hemsworth and Elsa Pataky have turned a coastal property in Byron Bay into a stunning modern mansion. The residence boasts a breathtaking 50-meter infinity pool, a fully equipped gym, and expansive outdoor areas for leisure. Recent upgrades include a tennis court and a dirt-bike track, enhancing the estate's allure.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2014-chris-hemsworth-bought-a-10-acre-australian-estate-for-a7-million-and-demolished-its-eight-bedroom-house-by-2026-the-rebuilt-compound-had-a-50-metre-pool-tennis-court-and-dirt-bike-track/articleshow/135199443.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2014-chris-hemsworth-bought-a-10-acre-australian-estate-for-a7-million-and-demolished-its-eight-bedroom-house-by-2026-the-rebuilt-compound-had-a-50-metre-pool-tennis-court-and-dirt-bike-track/articleshow/135199443.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T00:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135199466,imgsize-939076.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas man excluded from mother's will loses 70-acre property battle after court ruling]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135207043.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Texas couple have lost their legal battle to remain on 70 acres of land they say had been in their family for decades. The dispute began after William Dan Moss was excluded from his mother's will. Despite challenging the inheritance decision and subsequent eviction, William and his wife, Brenda, failed to overturn the rulings. On October 22, a Texas appeals court upheld the eviction judgment.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-couple-lose-possession-of-70-acres-after-mans-mother-excluded-him-from-her-will-appeals-court-upholds-eviction-ruling-involving-property-held-by-family-for-decades/articleshow/135207043.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-couple-lose-possession-of-70-acres-after-mans-mother-excluded-him-from-her-will-appeals-court-upholds-eviction-ruling-involving-property-held-by-family-for-decades/articleshow/135207043.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T00:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135207458,imgsize-291574.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists identify mushroom linked to visions of hundreds of tiny, colourful humans]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135199799.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The intriguing connection between the mushroom species Lanmaoa asiatica and hallucinations has come to light, particularly among users in China and the Philippines. Individuals describe encounters with small figures, a shared vision across multiple cultures. While the inquiry dates back to 1934, current advancements in identifying mushrooms provide fresh biological insights.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/for-100-plus-years-people-in-distant-parts-of-the-world-have-reported-seeing-hundreds-of-tiny-colourful-humans-after-eating-certain-wild-mushrooms-and-scientists-say-they-have-now-identified-the-mushroom-behind-it/articleshow/135199799.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/for-100-plus-years-people-in-distant-parts-of-the-world-have-reported-seeing-hundreds-of-tiny-colourful-humans-after-eating-certain-wild-mushrooms-and-scientists-say-they-have-now-identified-the-mushroom-behind-it/articleshow/135199799.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T23:24:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135199951,imgsize-1312245.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US court overturns $1.55 million judgment against couple who sought a $150,000 home price cut]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135216261.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Michigan appeals court has made headlines by overturning a hefty judgment against a couple who backed out of purchasing a luxury residence. Following an inspection that unveiled critical defects, the couple tried to renegotiate the price but ended up facing a breach of contract lawsuit. The trial court had favored the sellers, but the appeals court clarified the buyers' rights regarding inspection clauses, ultimately nullifying the ruling.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-michigan-couple-agreed-to-pay-1-275-million-for-a-home-but-sought-a-150000-discount-after-inspection-six-years-later-an-october-23-court-overturned-a-1-55-million-judgment-against-them/articleshow/135216261.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-michigan-couple-agreed-to-pay-1-275-million-for-a-home-but-sought-a-150000-discount-after-inspection-six-years-later-an-october-23-court-overturned-a-1-55-million-judgment-against-them/articleshow/135216261.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T22:52:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135216466,imgsize-1756841.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan appeals court orders protection order against Arizona father cancelled in custody dispute]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135216505.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A father in Arizona has successfully appealed a protection order placed against him by his child's mother. The Michigan Court of Appeals reversed an earlier court decision and ordered the protection order to be canceled. This dispute arose after the mother moved to Michigan with their child, preventing scheduled parenting time. The appeals court found that the mother did not provide sufficient evidence for the protection order.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-arizona-father-repeatedly-travelled-to-michigan-to-see-his-child-under-a-custody-order-but-the-mother-obtained-a-protection-order-accusing-him-of-harassment-an-october-23-appeals-court-ordered-that-protection-order-cancelled/articleshow/135216505.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-arizona-father-repeatedly-travelled-to-michigan-to-see-his-child-under-a-custody-order-but-the-mother-obtained-a-protection-order-accusing-him-of-harassment-an-october-23-appeals-court-ordered-that-protection-order-cancelled/articleshow/135216505.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T23:00:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135216633,imgsize-806880.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Halle Berry helps select filmmakers for Tribeca-Chanel program, awarding $120,000 for a short film]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135216769.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Halle Berry participated in a mentorship panel in New York City, selecting five teams to empower women and non-binary filmmakers through guidance and financial support. Among the winners were Gem Little and Kseniya Yorsh, awarded for their short film, COWARDS. The program not only offered workshops but also ensured ongoing assistance for project completion. Applications will be reopened prior to the 2027 Tribeca Festival.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-september-2026-halle-berry-joined-a-jury-choosing-five-emerging-women-filmmakers-for-tribeca-and-chanels-programme-the-winner-received-120000-to-make-a-short-film-while-four-others-earned-10000-grants/articleshow/135216769.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-september-2026-halle-berry-joined-a-jury-choosing-five-emerging-women-filmmakers-for-tribeca-and-chanels-programme-the-winner-received-120000-to-make-a-short-film-while-four-others-earned-10000-grants/articleshow/135216769.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T23:09:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135216992,imgsize-947343.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[ICE removes illegal immigrant Kanand Ojha from US over 2015 murder case in Guyana]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135216201.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ice-removes-illegal-immigrant-kanand-ojha-from-us-over-2015-murder-case-in-guyana/articleshow/135216201.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ice-removes-illegal-immigrant-kanand-ojha-from-us-over-2015-murder-case-in-guyana/articleshow/135216201.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T22:45:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135216253,imgsize-30728.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Started in 1969 for his children, Jack Klingbeil’s miniature railway grew into a family attraction]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135215804.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Wasilla, Alaska, a charming miniature railway stretches 3.5 miles, proudly family-run since 1969. This enchanting railroad features tunnels, bridges, and whimsical scale-model towns, captivating visitors of all ages. As a nonprofit organization, it thrives on volunteer support, offering memorable train rides, including a special chair car for those with special needs. Donations and volunteer efforts are vital for its ongoing maintenance and potential expansions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1969-jack-klingbeil-and-his-wife-started-a-miniature-railway-for-their-children-in-alaska-by-2026-it-had-grown-into-a-public-family-attraction-with-3-5-miles-of-track-bridges-and-tunnels-across-18-acres/arti