d over $1.1 million in six years, with 625 homes expected to participate in 2026. Now in its seventh year, the initiative aims to reach its overall $2 million fundraising goal.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-jeff-robertson-turned-his-halloween-skeleton-display-into-a-1-1-million-fundraiser-for-st-jude-childrens-research-hospital-now-625-homes-aim-to-raise-2-million-in-2026/articleshow/135215573.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-jeff-robertson-turned-his-halloween-skeleton-display-into-a-1-1-million-fundraiser-for-st-jude-childrens-research-hospital-now-625-homes-aim-to-raise-2-million-in-2026/articleshow/135215573.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T22:11:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135215700,imgsize-200777.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bowl For Ronnie: Ronnie James Dio cancer fund raises over $2m for research]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135210639.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ronnie-james-dio-cancer-fund-has-raised-more-than-2-million-since-his-death-backing-research-into-early-detection-and-treatment-of-prostate-colon-and-stomach-cancers/articleshow/135210639.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ronnie-james-dio-cancer-fund-has-raised-more-than-2-million-since-his-death-backing-research-into-early-detection-and-treatment-of-prostate-colon-and-stomach-cancers/articleshow/135210639.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T22:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135210713,imgsize-758988.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A wrong turn in Georgia led an Alabama driver to rescue a sleeping family of 14 from a house fire]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135215411.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A driver named Mr. Casey took a wrong turn in Georgia and discovered a house fire. He alerted the Burke family, which included 14 members, enabling them to escape safely. Despite their escape, the blaze destroyed their home and personal belongings completely. Community support has been overwhelming, with many offering clothing and shelter to the displaced family. The Burkes plan to rebuild and continue fostering children after establishing permanent housing.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-driver-headed-home-to-alabama-took-a-wrong-turn-in-georgia-and-spotted-a-house-on-fire-then-rushed-inside-to-wake-a-sleeping-family-of-14-the-couple-say-they-have-fostered-more-than-500-children-over-15-years/articleshow/135215411.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-driver-headed-home-to-alabama-took-a-wrong-turn-in-georgia-and-spotted-a-house-on-fire-then-rushed-inside-to-wake-a-sleeping-family-of-14-the-couple-say-they-have-fostered-more-than-500-children-over-15-years/articleshow/135215411.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T22:10:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135215779,imgsize-1811290.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why do people overpay for used cars with mileage just below round numbers?]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135209780.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A recent study showed that used car dealers profit from mileage readings just under round-number thresholds. The researchers analyzed millions of transactions to determine pricing impacts of left-digit bias. Buyers often overlook minor differences in mileage, focusing instead on the first digit. This inattention allows dealers to charge more for cars that appear to be better value.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/why-do-people-overpay-for-used-cars-with-mileage-just-below-round-numbers-researchers-examining-texas-car-transactions-found-that-dealers-earned-46-to-168-extra-at-certain-mileage-thresholds/articleshow/135209780.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/why-do-people-overpay-for-used-cars-with-mileage-just-below-round-numbers-researchers-examining-texas-car-transactions-found-that-dealers-earned-46-to-168-extra-at-certain-mileage-thresholds/articleshow/135209780.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T16:41:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135210062,imgsize-1032802.cms"/></item></channel></rss>